  partName: Right Inner Cover
  description: The Center Inner Cover is a large, elongated part positioned at the
    middle-center-center of the engine, constructed from Inside cover1 material.
    Its primary function is to enclose and protect the engine's central components,
    maintaining a stable and secure environment. Notably, its central location enables
    it to provide uniform support and coverage to the surrounding components.
